        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Russia deploys hypersonic missile in latest major strikes on Ukraine Europe Issued on: 25/05/2026 - 17:51 Kyiv is still dealing with the aftermath of a large-scale Russian overnight strike that killed four people and injured dozens, with emergency teams continuing search and cleanup operations across the city. More than 50 sites were hit, including homes, a school and a museum, while Russia says it used its Oreshnik hypersonic missile for only the third time in the war. Moscow describes the attacks as retaliation, while Ukraine denies targeting civilians and says its strikes focus on military infrastructure. Pope Leo warns AI must be “disarmed” in landmark encyclical 25/05/2026 Europe Pope Leo’s first encyclical tackles artificial intelligence 25/05/2026 Europe The mullet makes a comeback at European championship 25/05/2026 Europe 'We don't know what the death toll among military personnel is': Kyiv reels from Russian strikes 24/05/2026 Europe War in Ukraine: Russia launches massive missile strike on Kyiv 24/05/2026 Europe Protesters clash with police after an anti-government rally in Serbia's capital 24/05/2026 Europe War in Ukraine: Russian strikes hit a school killing one person 24/05/2026 Europe Russia says 16 killed in strike on student dorm that it blamed on Ukraine 23/05/2026 Europe Mexico, EU sign stalled trade deal as they aim to diversify from US 23/05/2026 Americas"
